  "notes": [
    "The Synty building kit placed from the Docks tile map -- read by render3d/static_pieces.cpp.",
    "pieces: role -> {pack, file} under content/art/lot-3d/static (gitignored, licensed). A role missing here, or a file missing on disk, leaves the chunk mesh's own atlas face standing.",
    "width/height/thickness are the piece's own module in metres (1 m = 1 tile; a storey is 3). front is the local side that wears the outdoor finish (-z = the brick of the Generic walls; +z = a cornice or lamp that hangs on the outside). standoff is how far the piece's local z=0 sits proud of the face it dresses (walls: half their thickness).",
    "extent is a flat piece's local footprint [minX, minZ, maxX, maxZ], fitted to rectangles of whole tiles between minBlock and maxBlock on a side (a patterned piece wants 2..3 so its stones stay stones; a plank or a flat fill takes any rectangle). flipY mirrors a downward-facing quad upward (the plaster ceiling laid as a floor). lift is metres above the surface. tint multiplies the light (255 = the piece's own colours). maxDistance is the cheap cull in tiles.",
    "materials: a tile material id (content/raws/materials) -> wall class (masonry: brick out, plaster in; timber: plaster both sides; none: chunk face), finish (brick, or plaster for a rendered stone building -- no brick corner piece on those), the outward tint, the indoor plaster tint (insideTint), the band below which its walls stay chunk, the floor piece its FLOOR cells wear (+ floorTint) and the flat fill (+ fillTint) laid over the cells the floor piece could not fit.",
    "minBand: nothing is placed below this band (the harbour's substrate). windowEvery: one outdoor masonry wall piece in this many is the window wall (0 = none). props.every: one floor cell against exactly one wall in this many gets a prop, split barrel/crate/sack by percent."
  ],
